const COPY_PLAYBOOK = `
PRIME DIRECTIVE: Copy does not create desire — it channels existing desire. Start where the customer's mind already is (what they want, believe, and have already tried and failed at). The market is the horse, copy is the reins.

AWARENESS ALIGNMENT: Every line must match the buyer's awareness level — Unaware → Problem Aware → Solution Aware → Product Aware → Most Aware. A Product-Aware headline written to a Problem-Aware market dies silently.

MARKET SOPHISTICATION: Mature markets demand a NEW MECHANISM, not a bigger promise. Name and brand the mechanism. "A new explanation / new process / new reason this works NOW." People don't buy what it is — they buy why it works. Destroy the old way, then reveal the real reason. Pattern: Old belief → Why it fails → New mechanism → Proof → Inevitability.

VALUE EQUATION: Value = (Dream Outcome × Perceived Likelihood) / (Time Delay × Effort & Sacrifice). Attack all four variables: bigger dream, more certain, faster, easier. Price is never the problem — weak value is.

OFFER ARCHITECTURE: A price is a number, an offer is a decision architecture. Make it feel stupid to say no. Core outcome + speed accelerator + risk reversal + objection-killing bonuses + scarcity with logic + a name that frames value. If it can be directly compared, it's weak.

PRESSURE WINS: Call out the reader directly. Challenge their excuses. Polarise hard. Stack proof until resistance collapses. Controlled arrogance — earned through proof, not ego.

HEADLINE RULES: Feels dangerous to ignore, personally relevant, slightly confrontational. The headline's job is to select the right reader — if everyone likes it, nobody buys.

BODY COPY = BELIEF SEQUENCING (not persuasion):
1. Agree with their pain.
2. Validate their skepticism.
3. Destroy false solutions.
4. Introduce the mechanism.
5. Prove it works.
6. Make the outcome inevitable.
Short lines. One idea per paragraph. Relentless forward motion.

PROOF IS NOT OPTIONAL: Numbers, case studies, before/after logic, process transparency, third-party validation. Proof doesn't add credibility — it replaces doubt.

CTA: Command, don't ask. "Get access now" / "Book your slot" / "Start here". The CTA should feel like relief, not pressure.

LANGUAGE: 3rd-grade reading level. Active voice only. Kill adverbs. Short sentences. Positive framing. Bad: "This program is very effective." Good: "This works."

DESTROY ALTERNATIVES (with logic, not insults): Why DIY fails. Why agencies fail. Why cheap options fail. Why the old method fails.

SALES PAGE STRUCTURE (Sell Like Crazy DNA):
1. Pre-head / eyebrow line that calls out the exact audience.
2. Magnetic headline + subheadline that deliver a specific big promise with tangible data, social proof, and a mechanism.
3. Identification / "You are here" paragraph that mirrors their current pain back to them in their own words.
4. Agitation: the cost of staying where they are.
5. The Godfather Offer reveal — named, stacked, risk-reversed, time-bound.
6. The "new mechanism" explanation: why every other approach fails and why this works NOW.
7. Proof stack: numbers, case studies, screenshots, testimonials, before/afters, credibility signals.
8. Deep benefit bullets (curiosity + specificity — "fascinations"), not features.
9. FAQ that handles the top 6–10 objections head-on, written as if you were already in a sales conversation.
10. Scarcity with logic (capacity, seasonality, cohort size).
11. Closing argument that paints the two futures: 90 days from now with vs. without this.
12. Direct, commanding CTA repeated — with a visible risk-reversal / guarantee underneath.

TONE: Edgy, direct, slightly confrontational, zero corporate fluff, zero "in today's fast-paced world" filler. Feel like a sharp, cocky, highly-successful operator is pulling the reader's collar, not a marketing intern.
`.trim();

portalRouter.post("/portal/sales-page-copy/headlines", requireAuth, async (req: any, res) => {
  try {
    const user = req.portalUser;
    const extraNotes = String(req.body?.extraNotes || "").slice(0, 2000);

    const [brainRow] = await db.select().from(userBrainProfilesTable).where(eq(userBrainProfilesTable.userId, user.id));
    const brain = resolveEffectiveBrain(brainRow, getPortalKey(req));
    const [lowTicketOffer] = await db.select({
      title: userAssetsTable.title, content: userAssetsTable.content,
    }).from(userAssetsTable)
      .where(and(eq(userAssetsTable.userId, user.id), eq(userAssetsTable.category, "low-ticket-build")))
      .orderBy(desc(userAssetsTable.createdAt)).limit(1);

    const brainContext = `
Business Owner: ${brain?.name || "Not specified"}
Company: ${brain?.companyName || "Not specified"}
Who They Help: ${brain?.whoDoYouHelp || "Not specified"}
How They Help Them: ${brain?.howDoYouHelpThem || "Not specified"}
Key Achievements / Results: ${brain?.keyAchievements || "Not specified"}
`.trim();

    const offerBlock = lowTicketOffer
      ? `SAVED LOW-TICKET OFFER:\n${lowTicketOffer.title}\n${(lowTicketOffer.content || "").replace(/<[^>]+>/g, " ").replace(/\s+/g, " ").slice(0, 5000)}`
      : "(No saved low-ticket offer on file — write from the brain profile.)";

    const extraNotesBlock = extraNotes
      ? `MANDATORY OWNER DIRECTIVES — these are the SINGLE MOST IMPORTANT inputs. Every single one of the 9 headlines or its subheadline MUST visibly use the specific numbers, results, time-frames, audience details, or angles supplied here. If the owner gave a number (e.g. "$724k/mo", "57k/day", "30,000 experts", "90 minutes"), at least 6 of the 9 headlines must surface that exact number verbatim or its bold equivalent. If the owner named an audience or mechanism, every headline must speak to that audience. Do NOT paraphrase the numbers softly — feature them.\n\nOWNER'S NOTES (verbatim):\n"""\n${extraNotes}\n"""`
      : "";

    const systemPrompt = `You are a world-class direct-response copywriter writing magnetic sales page headlines. You write ONLY in the style, rhythm, and cadence of the 9 reference examples provided. Do not invent new formats. Every headline must mimic the DNA of at least one of the 9 examples.

PRIORITY ORDER FOR INPUT (highest first):
1. MANDATORY OWNER DIRECTIVES (if present) — non-negotiable, must show up across the 9 outputs as described.
2. SAVED LOW-TICKET OFFER — the offer being sold.
3. BRAIN PROFILE — background context for tone and audience.

If the owner directives contradict the brain profile, the owner directives win.

HARD RULES:
- Stay ruthlessly within the stylistic parameters of the 9 examples.
- Every headline must include at least one of: (a) a specific tangible number/stat, (b) a social-proof figure, (c) a named mechanism, (d) a time-bound specific promise, (e) a clearly named objection being crushed.
- When owner directives include specific numbers, prefer those exact numbers over anything from the brain profile. Do not invent new numbers when the owner has supplied them.
- Subheadlines must expand the promise with additional proof, a mechanism, or an objection handled — not restate the headline.
- Vary across the 9 outputs: some headline-led, some bold-stated in CAPS, some question-led, some challenge-led, some "steal our X" framed, some DFY framed.
- NEVER mention the names of any copywriter, author, guru, book, agency, or third party (including but not limited to: Sabri, Suby, Sabri Suby, Sell Like Crazy, King Kong, Hormozi, Alex Hormozi, Schwartz, Eugene Schwartz, Breakthrough Advertising). The buyer must never see these names.
- NEVER use placeholder tokens like [TOKEN], {bracket} or TBD. Every headline must be fully written, deployable copy using the user's business context.
- Return ONLY valid JSON. No preamble, no trailing commentary.

OUTPUT FORMAT — return exactly this JSON shape:
{"items":[{"headline":"...","subheadline":"...","style":"short 2-3 word label e.g. 'Mechanism Flex' / 'Challenge' / 'Steal Our Playbook'"}]}
Return exactly 9 items.`;

    const userPrompt = `${extraNotesBlock ? extraNotesBlock + "\n\n" : ""}BUSINESS CONTEXT (BRAIN PROFILE):
${brainContext}

${offerBlock}

REFERENCE EXAMPLES (the ONLY stylistic universe you are allowed to write inside):
${PROVEN_HEADLINE_EXAMPLES}

Write 9 distinct headline+subheadline pairs for this business's low-ticket sales page. Mix the 9 stylistic directions across the reference examples.${extraNotesBlock ? " Remember: the OWNER DIRECTIVES at the top of this message are mandatory — every output must demonstrably use them, especially any specific numbers." : ""} Return the JSON only.`;

    const openai = new OpenAI({
      baseURL: process.env.AI_INTEGRATIONS_OPENAI_BASE_URL,
      apiKey: process.env.AI_INTEGRATIONS_OPENAI_API_KEY,
    });

    const completion = await openai.chat.completions.create({
      model: "gpt-4o",
      messages: [
        { role: "system", content: systemPrompt },
        { role: "user", content: userPrompt },
      ],
      response_format: { type: "json_object" },
      temperature: 0.9,
      max_tokens: 3500,
    });

    const raw = completion.choices[0]?.message?.content || "{}";
    let parsed: any = {};
    try { parsed = JSON.parse(raw); } catch { parsed = { items: [] }; }
    const items = Array.isArray(parsed.items) ? parsed.items.slice(0, 9) : [];
    res.json({ items });
    return;
  } catch (e: any) {
    console.error("sales-page-copy/headlines error:", e);
    res.status(500).json({ error: e?.message || "Failed to generate headlines" });
    return;
  }
});

async function buildLowTicketCopyContext(userId: number, portalKey: string = "main") {
  const [brainRow] = await db.select().from(userBrainProfilesTable).where(eq(userBrainProfilesTable.userId, userId));
  const brain = resolveEffectiveBrain(brainRow, portalKey);
  const [lowTicketOffer] = await db.select({
    title: userAssetsTable.title, content: userAssetsTable.content,
  }).from(userAssetsTable)
    .where(and(eq(userAssetsTable.userId, userId), eq(userAssetsTable.category, "low-ticket-build")))
    .orderBy(desc(userAssetsTable.createdAt)).limit(1);

  const researchDocs = await db.select({
    title: userAssetsTable.title, content: userAssetsTable.content,
  }).from(userAssetsTable)
    .where(and(eq(userAssetsTable.userId, userId), eq(userAssetsTable.category, "research-docs")))
    .orderBy(desc(userAssetsTable.createdAt)).limit(8);

  const stripHtml = (s: string) => (s || "").replace(/<[^>]+>/g, " ").replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim();

  const confirmed: any = brain?.confirmedLowTicketOffer || {};
  const _premiumRaw: any = brain?.confirmedPremiumOffer;
  const _premiumList: any[] = !_premiumRaw ? [] : (Array.isArray(_premiumRaw) ? _premiumRaw : [_premiumRaw]);
  const premium: any = _premiumList.find((o) => o && (o.name || o.price)) || {};

  const brainContext = `
Business Owner: ${brain?.name || "Not specified"}
Company: ${brain?.companyName || "Not specified"}
Niche / Sub-Niche: ${(brain as any)?.niche || ""}${(brain as any)?.subNiche ? ` / ${(brain as any).subNiche}` : ""}
Who They Help: ${brain?.whoDoYouHelp || "Not specified"}
How They Help Them: ${brain?.howDoYouHelpThem || "Not specified"}
Key Achievements / Results / Specific Numbers: ${brain?.keyAchievements || "Not specified"}
Unique Angle: ${(brain as any)?.uniqueAngle || "Not specified"}
Brand Colours: primary ${brain?.brandColorPrimary || "(unset)"}, secondary ${brain?.brandColorSecondary || "(unset)"}
Website: ${brain?.website || "(none)"}
`.trim();

  const generatedBrainBlock = brain?.generatedBrain
    ? `OWNER'S FULL CREATIVE STORY / GENERATED BRAIN (use this for tone, story arc, the "why behind the offer", the founder's voice, awareness positioning, market category framing — quote it where useful, never invent on top of it):\n${stripHtml(brain.generatedBrain).slice(0, 8000)}`
    : "(Owner has not generated their brain yet — fall back to the business context fields above.)";

  const offerBlock = lowTicketOffer
    ? `SAVED LOW-TICKET OFFER DOCUMENT (FULL — this is the canonical offer description, mechanism, deliverables, transformation, bonuses, guarantee, and pricing the page must sell):\n${lowTicketOffer.title}\n${stripHtml(lowTicketOffer.content || "").slice(0, 8000)}`
    : "(No saved low-ticket offer on file — leave clearly-marked TODOs anywhere a specific offer detail is needed.)";

  const confirmedOfferStack = `CONFIRMED OFFER STACK (use these EXACT names + prices verbatim wherever the page references the offer, bumps, upsells, downsell):
• Main Low-Ticket Offer: ${confirmed.offerName || "(not set)"} ${confirmed.offerPrice ? `at ${confirmed.offerPrice}` : ""}
• Order Bump 1: ${confirmed.orderBump1Name || "(not set)"} ${confirmed.orderBump1Price ? `at ${confirmed.orderBump1Price}` : ""}
• Order Bump 2: ${confirmed.orderBump2Name || "(not set)"} ${confirmed.orderBump2Price ? `at ${confirmed.orderBump2Price}` : ""}
• Upsell 1: ${confirmed.upsell1Name || "(not set)"} ${confirmed.upsell1Price ? `at ${confirmed.upsell1Price}` : ""}
• Downsell 1 (shown if buyer skips Upsell 1): ${confirmed.downsell1Name || "(not set)"} ${confirmed.downsell1Price ? `at ${confirmed.downsell1Price}` : ""}
• Upsell 2: ${confirmed.upsell2Name || "(not set)"} ${confirmed.upsell2Price ? `at ${confirmed.upsell2Price}` : ""}
• Upsell 3: ${confirmed.upsell3Name || "(not set)"} ${confirmed.upsell3Price ? `at ${confirmed.upsell3Price}` : ""}
• Premium / Backend Offer (used for thank-you upsell nudge): ${premium.offerName || premium.name || "(not set)"} ${premium.price ? `at ${premium.price}` : ""}`;

  const researchBlock = researchDocs.length
    ? `RESEARCH DOCS THE OWNER HAS GENERATED IN THIS PLATFORM (avatars, awareness stages, marketing angles, market research, etc. — feed these into avatar pain language, hooks, awareness-stage framing, mechanism naming, and competitor differentiation):\n` +
      researchDocs.map(d => `• ${d.title}\n  ${stripHtml(d.content || "").slice(0, 1400)}`).join("\n\n")
    : "(No research docs on file yet — owner has not generated avatars / angles / market research.)";

  return { brain, confirmed, premium, brainContext, offerBlock, researchBlock, generatedBrainBlock, confirmedOfferStack };
}

const SHARED_TONE_RULES = `- Tone: edgy, direct, confrontational, zero corporate filler, zero "in today's fast-paced world" clichés, short punchy sentences. No em or en dashes anywhere in the final copy.
- NEVER mention any copywriter, author, guru, agency, or book by name (including: Sabri, Suby, Sabri Suby, Sell Like Crazy, King Kong, Hormozi, Alex Hormozi, Schwartz, Eugene Schwartz, Breakthrough Advertising). The final copy and the prompt itself must never expose these names.
- Do not fabricate specific numbers, testimonials, or client names that weren't provided. Where specifics are needed, use the owner's own numbers from the business context. If a proof asset is genuinely missing, instruct the coding agent to leave a clearly-commented TODO block at that exact spot.
- Output plain text. No markdown code fences around the whole thing. No markdown bold (**) inside the copy itself. Use clear section headers the coding agent can follow.
- BE EXHAUSTIVE within the EXISTING sections. The owner pastes this ONCE and the coding agent rewrites every visible piece of copy on the page in a single shot. No back-and-forth.
- For EVERY listed section, supply the FINAL HEADLINE TEXT, the FINAL SUBHEAD/BODY TEXT, every bullet, every button label, every microcopy line. No placeholders like "[insert X]" except where genuinely missing owner data — in which case use a TODO comment, never a vague placeholder.

CRITICAL — REWRITE ONLY, NO STRUCTURAL CHANGES:
- The page already has its full layout. Your job is ONLY to swap the visible TEXT inside the sections that are listed in the section map below.
- DO NOT add any new sections, blocks, headings, testimonials, "as seen in" logos, social proof rows, FAQ blocks, comparison tables, guarantee boxes, footers, trust bars, security badges, or anything else that is not explicitly listed in the section map.
- DO NOT remove any sections that ARE listed in the section map. The number of sections out must equal the number of sections in.
- DO NOT touch JSX structure, components, imports, image src paths, className strings, inline styles, hooks, useState, useEffect, route handlers, button onClick handlers, payment wiring, form validation, or any logic. The git diff after the agent finishes must be a pure copy-text swap, nothing else.
- If a section in the map references something the owner has not provided (e.g. a guarantee length, a specific number, a testimonial name), leave a clearly-commented \`// TODO: …\` inside that section — do NOT invent content and do NOT delete the section.`;

const OWNER_ADDENDUM_HEADER = (pageLabel: string) => `OWNER DIRECTIVE (READ THIS FIRST — DO NOT SKIP):
For the ${pageLabel}, follow these instructions exactly. Use any fixed headline / subheadline VERBATIM where given. Rewrite the WHOLE PAGE — every section listed in the section map below, every line of body copy, every bullet, every CTA, every microcopy snippet — to match the owner's offer, audience, branding, and creative story.

The owner has loaded their research docs (avatar angles, market awareness stages, marketing hooks, market research) and their full low-ticket offer document into this Replit workspace. READ those files first as authoritative context for the avatar's pain language and the offer's exact mechanics. If anything in those uploaded docs conflicts with this prompt, the docs win.`;

